{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"41662dd8-2973-48ad-b20f-a72bc427d6de","status":"SUCCESS","response":"Prisma ORM has been added and configured for the project.\n\n### Summary of Actions\n\n1. **Installed Prisma ORM Packages**:\n   - Installed the current version of Prisma from npm (`prisma@8.0.0-rc.33`, `@prisma/orm-postgres`, `@prisma/cli-engine`, and `dotenv`).\n   - Scaffolded the configuration via `npx prisma orm init --target postgres --authoring psl`.\n\n2. **Modeled Schema (`User` \u0026 `Post`)**:\n   - Configured [`src/prisma/contract.prisma`](file:///tmp/h-PgToj1/src/prisma/contract.prisma):\n     - **`User`**: `id` (autoincrement PK), `email` (unique string), `name` (optional string), `posts` (`Post[]`).\n     - **`Post`**: `id` (autoincrement PK), `title` (string), `content` (optional string), `published` (boolean default `false`), `author` (`User`), and `authorId` (`Int`).\n   - Emitted the contract types and runtime metadata using `npx prisma contract emit`.\n\n3. **Created Database Tables**:\n   - Created tables in the local PostgreSQL database specified in `.env` using `npx prisma db init`.\n   - Verified that the `User` and `Post` tables, relations, and indexes were created and synced.\n\n4. **Added Execution Script**:\n   - Created [`script.ts`](file:///tmp/h-PgToj1/script.ts) at the root, which creates a user with two posts, queries all users together with their posts (`db.orm.public.User.include('posts').all()`), prints the results, and cleans up the connection.\n   - Tested and verified with `npx tsx script.ts`.\n\n5. **Documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-PgToj1/ANSWER.md)**:\n   - Detailed the setup steps, model definitions, and script execution instructions.\n","duration_seconds":362.176352,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":355101,"output_tokens":5633,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":2734575,"total_tokens":360734}}}
